Ni bulk hosts at nsp=2 for the Ni(001) surface decks ni001_soc_u3 and ni001_soc_u0. Recipe of ni001_u3/bulk_input.nml (RS Chebyshev, lld=200, 2500 channels, rc=100, beta 0.05 Broyden, ldm_beta 0.3) with nsp=2; the host potential files are in the surface decks. Edited lines only:
input_b0.nml: nsp=2, no U (hubbard lines removed), fermi -0.061969 (start value); seed Ni.nml of ni001_u0.
input_b1.nml: nsp=2, U=3/J=0.7 local, SOC on; seed Ni.nml + Ni_dm.nml of ni001_u3 (nsp=1 host).
input_b2.nml: as b1 with soc_scale=0 and fix_soc; seed as b1.

Runs stopped early by choice (no convergence study); numbers are per-step values from the log (d trace, spin moment mspin in muB, |L| orbital moment in muB, max |P_up,dn| of the spinor d density matrix):
b2 (SOC->0): converged at step 5, Diff 9.9e-9; mspin 0.766354, d trace 8.5905, host differs from the nsp=1 U=3 host by at most 1.8e-8 in any potential parameter (gravity_center), E_F -0.076743.
b1 (SOC on): stopped after step 7. Diff 9.9e-5, 9.8e-5, 9.7e-5, 9.6e-5, 5.0e-5, 8.0e-5, 7.8e-5. |L| 0.0446, 0.0504, 0.0551, 0.0589, 0.0620, 0.0645, 0.0665 (still rising, increments 5.8e-3 falling to 2.0e-3 per step); mspin 0.76584 -> 0.76543; d trace 8.59025 -> 8.59034; max |P_up,dn| 9.0e-3 -> 1.1e-2; E_F -0.076576.
b0 (U=0, SOC on): stopped after step 7. Diff 6.8e-4, 6.5e-4, 2.6e-4, 2.4e-4, 1.3e-4, 1.1e-4, 9.1e-5. |L| 0.04327 -> 0.04358; mspin 0.68382 -> 0.68817; E_F -0.063070.
The step-7 potential of b0 and b1 (Ni_scf.nml, Ni_dm.nml) is the host of ni001_soc_u0 / ni001_soc_u3/host_soc; it is not a converged state.
